      "Booklibre (formerly Colophon) collects no data. There is no account, no analytics, no advertising, no identifier.",
      "Your photos and albums stay on your computer. Composing and exporting the PDF happen offline.",
      "From the photo library, Booklibre copies the photos of the album you pick into a folder in your Pictures. It never changes or deletes anything there.",
      "The Mac App Store version calls no server.",
      "Prices. If you answer “Through Booklibre” to “How will you print it?”, the downloaded version reads the price table from prices.booklibre.app once each time it opens. The request carries no identifier and nothing of your album, not even the country you picked. “Myself” turns it off.",
      "Ordering. If you order a printed album (France only), Booklibre sends the relay api.booklibre.app the delivery country, the format, the page count, then the album’s two PDFs, so every photograph in it. The files are deleted at the latest 30 days after the order. If you agreed to print pages under 250 ppi, the list of those pages (numbers and resolutions, no photo name) is kept 180 days. To limit abuse, the relay counts requests per hashed IP address, and deletes that count after two days.",
